{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1539795567,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzExNzU5OTI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2930","origin":"github"},"title":"Exclude 'notneeded' messages in default result renderer","message":"I somewhat remembered that @yarikoptic had proposed that before, but I cannot find the issue.\n\n**Rational**: `notneeded` results are reported when there is nothing to do or nothing was done, so from the perspective of an activity log there is nothing to report.\n\n**Counter argument**: When there is no progress bar, those message could serve as (the only) activity indicator. OTOH it is even simpler to send log messages feeding a progress bar than to compose a result record, so such cases could easily be RF'ed.\n\n**Clarification**: I do NOT propose to stop emitting `notneeded` results (those are essential, at least for me), but I want to suppress their rendering in the default renderer. This will not affect any custom rendering that may be implemented by particular commands.","files":null}]}